# 101. Symmetric Tree

## APPROACH: SYMMETRIC TREE (RECURSIVE / MIRROR DFS)

Idea:
Ek tree tabhi symmetric (apne center ke around mirror image) hota hai jab:
1. Root ke Left Subtree aur Right Subtree ek dusre ke mirror reflections hon.
2. Mirror ka rule:
   - Left subtree ka left child == Right subtree ka right child (Outers match).
   - Left subtree ka right child == Right subtree ka left child (Inners match).
   - Dono corresponding nodes ki values equal honi chahiye.

--------------------------------------------------

APPROACH (Recursive / DFS)

1. Edge Case:
   Agar `root == null` ho, toh tree naturally symmetric hota hai (`return true`).
   Otherwise, helper function call karo: `helper(root.left, root.right)`.

2. Helper Function `helper(left, right)`:
   - **Base Case 1 (Structural Null Check):**
     Agar dono me se koi bhi node `null` hai:
     `if (left == null || right == null) return (left == right);`
     *(Dono null hain toh `true` return hoga, agar ek null aur ek non-null hai toh mismatch hone par `false` return hoga).*

   - **Base Case 2 (Value Check):**
     Agar dono nodes ki value match nahi karti:
     `if (left.val != right.val) return false;`

   - **Recursive Calls (Mirror Check):**
     1. Outer branches compare karo: `helper(left.left, right.right)`
     2. Inner branches compare karo: `helper(left.right, right.left)`
     Dono conditions `true` aani chahiye:
     `return helper(left.left, right.right) && helper(left.right, right.left);`

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

Tree:
        1
       / \
      2   2
     / \ / \
    3  4 4  3

Dry Run:
- Root 1 -> helper(Node 2-Left, Node 2-Right)
- Values compare: 2 == 2 (Match!)
- Check 1 (Outers): helper(3, 3)
  - Values match (3 == 3)
  - Left & right of both are null -> returns true
- Check 2 (Inners): helper(4, 4)
  - Values match (4 == 4)
  - Left & right of both are null -> returns true
- Node 2 level returns true && true = true.

Result: true

--------------------------------------------------

WHY (left == right) SHORTCUT WORKS?

- `if (left == null || right == null)` par aane ka matlab hai kam se kam ek node `null` zaroor hai.
- Agar dono `null` hain, toh `left == right` evaluate hoke `true` de dega.
- Agar sirf ek `null` hai aur doosra valid node hai, toh `left == right` evaluate hoke `false` de dega.
- Yeh single-line clean syntax redundant `if-else` blocks ko replace karta hai.

--------------------------------------------------

COMPLEXITY

N = Total number of nodes in tree
H = Height of binary tree

Time:
O(N) -> Har node pair exactly ek baar visit aur compare hota hai. Short-circuit mismatch milte hi execution rok deta hai.

Space:
O(H) -> Recursive call stack tree ki height ke barabar memory leta hai.
Worst case (skewed tree): O(N)
Best/Average case (balanced tree): O(log N)

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW POINT

- Difference between Same Tree (LeetCode 100) and Symmetric Tree (LeetCode 101):
  - Same Tree me parallel traverse karte hain: `(p.left, q.left)` aur `(p.right, q.right)`.
  - Symmetric Tree me cross / mirror traverse karte hain: `(left.left, right.right)` aur `(left.right, right.left)`.
- Interviewer follow-up: *"Iterative approach kaise karoge?"*
  - **Iterative (Queue):** Ek `Queue<TreeNode>` lo. Starting me `queue.offer(root.left)` aur `queue.offer(root.right)` dalo. Loop me do-do nodes poll karke mirror order me children push karte jao: `(left.left, right.right)` then `(left.right, right.left)`.

--------------------------------------------------

# CODE:

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public boolean isSymmetric(TreeNode root) {
        // Root null hai toh symmetric hai, warna left aur right subtree mirror check karo
        return (root == null) || helper(root.left, root.right);        
    }

    private boolean helper(TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
        // Agar koi ek ya dono null hain: dono null honge toh true dega, ek null hoga toh false
        if (left == null || right == null) {
            return (left == right);
        }

        // Values match honi chahiye
        if (left.val != right.val) {
            return false;
        }

        // Mirror comparison: Outer pairs match && Inner pairs match
        return helper(left.left, right.right) && helper(left.right, right.left);
    }
}
